{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 6300,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is such an awesome experience"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8860,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To get up close and personal with the curiosity rover"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12140,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, this isn't the exact one that's on Mars, obviously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's basically identical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18200,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: I'm here at the Jet Propulsion Lab in Pasadena, California"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21840,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know how we got in here, Bill. It's amazing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24640,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: This is the NASA center that's famous for building things like the Mars rover,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28940,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space probes, and rescuing Matt Damon from the red planet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32620,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: You guys must get pretty sick of answering questions about The Martian"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35660,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36700,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: This is project scientist Ken Farley"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39420,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I spoke with him about life on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41700,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's one of many scientists working \non the first NASA mission in 40 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45810,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designed specifically to look for life on another planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49420,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called, Mars 2020."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51980,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: If there were life on Mars, wouldn't we have found it by now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55420,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: No. We would not have found it by now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57300,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: But we've been looking! There's been a number of missions like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59560,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Viking landers and like Curiosity, for example"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62860,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: Part of the problem is, we're not even sure what we're looking for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66580,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Life on Mars may have been completely\ndifferent from life on Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70980,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Recent missions, like the Curiosity and Exploration rovers, look for and found evidence of water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76580,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a key ingredient for life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78580,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SARAH: Follow the water, where was the water and when was the water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81420,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then looking for habitability, looking for places that could have supported life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86620,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we know enough about Mars\nto look for ancient life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89820,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of anything on the surface of Mars today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92740,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: There's no life on the surface of Mars today?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94740,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SARAH: Most likely, if there is life on Mars today, it would be underground, underneath the ice caps,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102060,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in places that are very very hard to investigate with the sort of rovers and landers that we've sent so far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107920,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: So we're talking, like, moles, groundhogs [LAUGHTER]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110520,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SARAH: Well, microscopic, bacterial moles. No, not actual moles!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115280,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're looking for, we call them biosignatures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117860,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a pattern or a substance in the rocks that can only have been formed by life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: To find those biosignatures, the 2020 rover is gonna need cutting edge technologies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126920,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developed here at JPL."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for definitive proof of life, they'll need drill samples."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134800,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: We need to take a core, that's about the size of a piece of chalk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have to collect 37 tubes like this that will ultimately be laid on the surface of Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142360,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for possible return in the future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144040,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: Mars 2020 is different from past missions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145940,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because now NASA will need to bring those samples back to Earth to test them for evidence of life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151880,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: If they are brought back to Earth, we will be able to use all sorts of different kinds of techniques,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156620,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many of which have not yet even been invented"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158680,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because nobody has been posed with this question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VOICEOVER: So, in order to find life, we'll have to return those samples from Mars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something that's never been done before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166880,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then test those samples with techniques that haven't even been invented yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170940,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I had to ask:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172440,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: How good do you think your chances are, of finding life?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174940,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: Hmmm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177480,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd say they're poorer than even just because I remain skeptical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regardless, we will learn about what the early history of the Solar System is like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186880,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's the same environment, the same Solar System, that earth was in when life was evolving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191100,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to understand the origin of life, on Earth 'cause that's the only place we know life exists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196600,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rocks that recorded that are all gone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199400,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DEREK: So in a way, looking at Mars is like looking at a version of Earth frozen in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right about when life would've sprung?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207960,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "KEN: That's, I think, the most exciting way to look at it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211020,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just unbelievable. The stuff that is happening here is just so far beyond anything else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216400,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What are you doing today?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217160,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are you sitting in your cubicle, are you working on your computer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219460,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, these guys are working on a freaking machine, in outer space, on Mars that is trying to discover life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227300,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228860,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That was one of my field pieces from the Netflix show \"Bill Nye Saves the World\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233120,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on which I am a correspondent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235080,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you haven't seen it, you should check it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237100,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, obviously, because that show is for a broader audience, I don't get to go into the kinda crazy detail"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242180,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I sometimes do on this channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244100,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, this image is the first ever beamed back from the Martian surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249040,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was taken by the Soviet lander, Mars 3 on\nDecember 2, 1971."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254300,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After becoming the first man-made object to make a soft landing on Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259300,
    "dDurationMs": 6980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that lander transmitted data back to earth for just 14.5 seconds before going quiet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266280,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And no one really knows what happened to it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268660,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it might have had something to do with the huge dust storm that was taking place at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272800,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is the first clear image sent back from the Martian surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276300,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was taken by the Viking One Lander on\nJuly 20th 1976."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280560,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one of the stated aims for that mission, was to try to find evidence of existing life on the Martian surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287060,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there was this experiment \ncalled the labeled release experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290080,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where a scoop of Martian soil was taken"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292060,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then a dilute solution of nutrients was\nadded into that soil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296900,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but, in those nutrients was the radioactive atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300220,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Carbon-14, the idea was if you tried"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303140,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to detect the gases around the soil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304980,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you detect some radioactive Carbon Dioxide"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307660,
    "dDurationMs": 1499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know that the nutrients were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309160,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "broken down by something in the soil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310860,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "presumably something that's living."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313140,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what was remarkable about this experiment was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314920,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it got a positive result, there were a few other experiments trying to detect life in other ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320160,
    "dDurationMs": 6220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they failed to get a detection, but this one\ndetected radioactive Carbon Dioxide"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326380,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what's even more impressive was the\nViking 2 Lander"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329400,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which tried the same experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331330,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the Viking 1 Lander, it also got"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333490,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same positive result, so things were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336000,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking promising, but then about a week"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338380,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "later they tried to rerun the experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340640,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "add a little bit more nutrients to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341860,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "soil and see if you could get more CO₂, but they couldn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346220,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was no additional CO₂ released, so based \non these negative results and the negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352320,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "results of the other experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353660,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most scientists have concluded that there is no surviving life on the surface of Mars, today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360500,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so how is the CO₂ produced in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, chemists suspect that very highly oxidizing chemicals, things like perchlorates, exist in the Martian"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "soil and would have reacted with \nthe nutrients producing the CO₂ to start with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373120,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, once those chemicals are used up, well there's nothing for those"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376480,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nutrients to react with, and so we get no"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378520,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "CO₂ the next time, the nutrients are introduced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381440,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this story highlights just how difficult searching\nfor life is using only remote instruments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386860,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why, for Mars 2020 they're going to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "create some rock samples that should be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391120,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "returned to earth, if only they can get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393260,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the budget for another mission that will go \nback and pick them up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396620,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the rover they're sending in 2020, will \nalso have some new tools on board"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400080,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that will allow them to look at rocks in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401660,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "finer detail than ever before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403960,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One tool called PIXL, will use x-ray spectrometry to try to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408580,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "detect chemical elements with a spatial resolution that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411040,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes down to the size of a grain of salt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413940,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now what they be looking for, are layered structures similar to stromatolite found here on earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419760,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those are mineral deposits which get\nbuilt up by billions and billions of-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424360,
    "dDurationMs": 7260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny organisms. - So you are not really looking for\nfossils or tiny little you know, microbial evidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431620,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are looking for the structures that they\nwould have produced, layered structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435180,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's how we know about the oldest life\non Earth, and so it's logical to think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's how we might find out about this old life on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the job of finding evidence of past\nor current life on Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444960,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is made even more difficult by Planetary Protection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448460,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's the principle whereby we\nshould not introduce any life from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452160,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Earth to these places where we're studying like Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454760,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's completely understandable, because I mean the worst discovery of life we could make on Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459700,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be life that we introduced there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462440,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by our spacecraft..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464200,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean certain organisms are really hardy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even in the vacuum of space and even when\nbombarded by radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, due to this constraint, spacecraft must be strenuously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474440,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sterilized and also, they're restricted from landing near sites where we think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478640,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there may be liquid water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479920,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm really looking forward to the results of\nthe Mars 2020 mission."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hopefully a later mission, where we actually go back and collect the samples that were placed there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487960,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one thing that really struck me from my interview with Kim Farley was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491100,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he said that Mars is really like a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492980,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time capsule of the rocks that Earth had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495320,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when life evolved here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497240,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's, a way I'd never really thought about it before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499940,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but of course because of plate tectonics and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the weathering that would have taken place on earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504040,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we don't have the rock record from when\nlife was first evolving on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508080,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this planet, and that makes Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509780,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a really good place to look, not only for new\nforms of life, but also for an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514300,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understanding of how life on Earth, may have begun."
    } ]
  } ]
}
